{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of scale, siting, design, bulk, mass and appearance would be an undesirable addition, representing an overly dominant and disproportionate extension to the dwelling.&nbsp; The side extension would sit uncomfortably to the side of the host dwelling, significantly impacting the character and symmetry of the semi-detached dwelling and failing to appear as subordinate. The subject site is located on a prominent corner plot and with the proposed side extension and front extension being significantly visible form public vantage points, and would be visually intrusive, represent poor design and would be out of character in the context of the area.&nbsp; As such,&nbsp; the proposal would cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the host dwelling and surrounding area, including the historic distinctiveness of the Becontree Estate. The proposal is therefore contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that development recognises local character and promotes good design whilst protecting and enhancing historic environments:&nbsp;- National Planning Policy Framework&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)- The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)-&nbsp;Policies SP2, DMD1, DMD4 and DMD5 of&nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037: (September 2024)"
  ],
